I have completed a thorough exploration. Here is my report on the Owner-related code in this Spring Boot REST project (Spring PetClinic REST).

## Overview

This is a Maven-based Spring Boot REST app. The single write endpoint under test is `POST /api/owners`. Notably, request/response DTOs are NOT hand-written — they are generated at build time by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto` (e.g. `OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`). The API interfaces (`OwnersApi`, `OwnerV2Api`) are generated into `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.api`.

## 1. Owner entity/model

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "owners")
public class Owner extends Person {
    @Column(name = "address") @NotEmpty private String address;
    @Column(name = "city") @NotEmpty private String city;
    @Column(name = "telephone") @NotEmpty
    @Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", message = "...E.164...") private String telephone;
    @Column(name = "email") private String email;
    @Column(name = "registration_date") private LocalDate registrationDate;
    @Column(name = "customer_code") private String customerCode;
    @OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL, mappedBy = "owner", fetch = FetchType.EAGER)
    private Set<Pet> pets;
    // getters/setters, pet helpers...
}
```

Base class `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java` (`@MappedSuperclass`) provides `firstName` and `lastName` (both `@NotEmpty`, columns `first_name` / `last_name`).

Important: There is NO `sharesHousehold` field on the entity. The only occurrence of `sharesHousehold` in the whole codebase is in the acceptance test (see section 6). There is also no notion of soft-delete / "deleted" flag despite the test helper's Javadoc mentioning one.

## 2. Owner controllers

V1 (main CRUD): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` — `@RestController @RequestMapping("/api")`, implements generated `OwnersApi`. The create endpoint:

```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

Also has `listOwners`, `getOwner`, `updateOwner`, `deleteOwner` (returns 204, not a soft-delete — calls `clinicService.deleteOwner`), plus pet/visit sub-resource endpoints.

V2 (read-only paging): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java` — only `listOwnersPage`.

Mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` (MapStruct). `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` ignores `id`/`pets`, normalizes telephone to E.164 via `TelephoneNormalizer.toE164`, normalizes email via `EmailNormalizer.normalize`. `toOwnerDto` computes `displayName`/`initials` via `PersonNameFormatter`.

## 3. Service layer

Interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java` — Owner methods: `findOwnerById`, `findAllOwners`, `findOwners(String,Pageable)`, `saveOwner`, `deleteOwner`, `findOwnerByLastName`.

Impl: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`. The create logic (this is where creation business rules live):

```java
@Override
@Transactional
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
    if (owner.isNew()) {
        if (ownerRepository.existsByTelephone(owner.getTelephone())) {
            throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(owner.getTelephone());
        }
        if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) {
            owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());
        }
        owner.setCustomerCode(
            CustomerCodeGenerator.format(owner.getLastName(), ownerRepository.count() + 1));
    }
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}
```

So the existing "conflict" rule is a duplicate-telephone check. There is currently NO lastName+address duplicate check and no household concept.

## 4. Repository (Spring Data JPA)

Interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java` — declares `findByLastName` (Collection and Page overloads), `findById(int)`, `existsByTelephone(String)`, `count()`, `save`, `findAll`, `delete`.

Active impl (profile `spring-data-jpa`, which is the default in both main and test config): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` extends `OwnerRepository, Repository<Owner,Integer>`, with `@Query` overrides including `existsByTelephone` (derived query) and a JPQL `findByLastName` using `LIKE :lastName%`.

Other (inactive-by-default) impls exist: `.../repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` and `.../repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java` — these implement the same `OwnerRepository` interface, so any new repository method added to the interface would need implementations there too (or those profiles would break).

## 5. Validation and error/409 handling

Bean Validation constraints live on the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (driven by the OpenAPI `OwnerFields` schema at `openapi.yml` lines 1991-2055): `firstName`/`lastName` letters-only patterns, `address` and `city` `minLength:1 maxLength` + `.*\S.*` pattern, `telephone` with custom `@TelephoneDigits`, `email` `@Email`, required = firstName,lastName,address,city,telephone.

Custom validators: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/` (`TelephoneDigits` + `TelephoneDigitsValidator`, `PetAgeValidation` + `PetAgeValidator`).

Global handler: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` (`@ControllerAdvice`, returns RFC-7807 `ProblemDetail`):
- `DuplicateTelephoneException` → 409 CONFLICT (`handleDuplicateTelephoneException`). This is the existing pattern to emulate for a new conflict rule.
- `MethodArgumentNotValidException` → 400 with `errors` + `schemaValidationErrors`.
- `DataIntegrityViolationException` → 404.
- `AccessDeniedException` re-thrown (so Security produces 403/401); generic `Exception` → 500.

Conflict exception: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/DuplicateTelephoneException.java` (extends `RuntimeException`). This is the template a household-duplicate exception would follow.

## 6. Existing Owner-creation tests

Directory: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/`

- `AcceptanceTest.java` — JUnit 5, black-box tests hitting real endpoints via MockMvc. Its class-level Javadoc says the checkpoint is "household-duplicate: Reject creating an owner when another owner has the same lastName and the same address". The three tests define the target behavior:
  - `coreRejectsSameLastNameAndAddress` — same lastName + same address → expect 409 Conflict.
  - `functionalityAllowsDifferentAddress` — same lastName, different address → 2xx.
  - `functionalityAllowsWithSharesHousehold` — same lastName + address but request body has `sharesHousehold: true` → 2xx. (This is the only reference to `sharesHousehold` anywhere; the field does not yet exist in the entity/DTO.)

- `AcceptanceBase.java` — abstract base: `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles={"OWNER_ADMIN",...})`. Provides `ownerNode()` (fully-unique valid owner JSON: firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone), `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk` (POST `/api/owners`), `getOwner`/`fetchOwner`, `extractId`, plus lots of unique-value generators and pinned reference data. Uses Jackson 3 (`tools.jackson.databind.*`). Note `createOwnerOk` asserts `is2xxSuccessful()` and the controller returns 201.

- `AuditLogCapture.java` — test support helper also references Owner.

There are no unit/`@WebMvcTest` tests specifically for `OwnerRestControllerV1`/service/repository; owner coverage is via these acceptance tests.

## 7. Build tool and running tests

- Build tool: Maven, with wrapper `/home/daniel/sandbox/mvnw` (and `mvnw.cmd`). POM: `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` (parent `spring-boot-starter-parent`).
- DTO/API generation: `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` 7.23.0, `inputSpec=src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, `generatorName=spring`, `apiPackage=org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.api`, `modelPackage=org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`. So changing request/response shape (e.g. adding `sharesHousehold`) requires editing `openapi.yml`, not editing generated Java. (Note: this is a read-only exploration; I did not modify anything.)
- Persistence profile: default `spring-data-jpa`; tests use `spring.profiles.active=hsqldb,spring-data-jpa` (`src/test/resources/application.properties`), main uses `h2,spring-data-jpa`.
- Run tests: `./mvnw test` (full build/verify: `./mvnw clean install`). Run app: `./mvnw spring-boot:run`.
- To run just the acceptance tests: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`.

## Key takeaways for an Owner-creation change

The existing 409 pattern to mirror: throw a `RuntimeException` subclass in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` (like `DuplicateTelephoneException`) and map it to `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`. Any new duplicate-detection query (e.g. exists-by-lastName-and-address) must be added to the `OwnerRepository` interface and implemented in all three repository impls (spring-data-jpa is the active one). A `sharesHousehold` input field would need to be added to the OpenAPI `OwnerFields` schema (regenerating `OwnerFieldsDto`) and carried through the `OwnerMapper` — it is currently absent everywhere except the acceptance test.

