- Persistence profile: default `spring-data-jpa`; tests use `spring.profiles.active=hsqldb,spring-data-jpa` (`src/test/resources/application.properties`), main uses `h2,spring-data-jpa`.
- Run tests: `./mvnw test` (full build/verify: `./mvnw clean install`). Run app: `./mvnw spring-boot:run`.
- To run just the acceptance tests: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`.

## Key takeaways for an Owner-creation change

The existing 409 pattern to mirror: throw a `RuntimeException` subclass in `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner` (like `DuplicateTelephoneException`) and map it to `HttpStatus.CONFLICT` in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`. Any new duplicate-detection query (e.g. exists-by-lastName-and-address) must be added to the `OwnerRepository` interface and implemented in all three repository impls (spring-data-jpa is the active one). A `sharesHousehold` input field would need to be added to the OpenAPI `OwnerFields` schema (regenerating `OwnerFieldsDto`) and carried through the `OwnerMapper` — it is currently absent everywhere except the acceptance test.

